    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The first Chinese dynasty known from its own writing, ruling the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> plain from c. 1600 to 1046 BCE.</li><li>Its kings divined with inscribed oracle bones, the oldest substantial body of Chinese writing.</li><li>Its bronze ritual vessels, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> and royal tombs at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anyang">Anyang</a> make it one of the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> civilisations.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Before scholars recognised the writing on them around 1899, Shang oracle bones were ground up and sold by apothecaries as 'dragon bones' for medicine.</p></aside>
    </section>

